Ticket #4471 is not one parser bug. The export has overlapping pages, so each report ID counts
once. A report's cause comes from its tenant's locale and booking form, not the browser-based
intake tag.

<Callout>
Two causes need two tickets. The parser and date-hint failures need different fixes.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Parser: month-first reading

The shared parser reads every date month first. For a day-first tenant, app, email and
booking-v2 form reports can flip the day and month. This remains the primary cause in #4471.

## Hint: contradictory format guidance

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, but reads the tenant's day-first format. Reports
through that form are the `hint` cause, even when intake tagged them `parser`.

## Triage note

Reports that read as a one-day move stay with the cause supplied by tenant and form; the desk
note does not make a third cause. Matching subjects explain the merge, not a shared root cause.

